# The annotations of the 128K hook stubs as they run at $B30D-$B3A8 (156 bytes, block 2's $610E-$61A9, copied there
# piece by piece by block 2's set-up, src/game/setup.asm): the single source of src/game/stubs*.asm
# (tools/part_mkasm.py). The image is work/parts/stubs-b30d.bin; the code is what the analysis build work/stage2/game
# (recording c1, frames 3313:51573-13702: the game menu and six games) ran, widened by mkgame's walk.
#
# The 48K game called its beeper (CALL $B2F0 with A = the sound) at each of these events; the set-up points those
# call sites (and a few instructions next to them) at the stubs. A stub does the site's own instruction where it
# replaced one, then starts one sound of the page-4 engine (src/sound/engine.asm) through HookSound. The events are
# docs/09-sound.md 9.2's.

@equ $5B50 MusicSwitch ; the glue: A = 0 stops the music, else starts it (src/game/glue.asm)
@equ $7FFD PORT_7FFD ; the 128K paging port
@equ $8072 ShipLostFlag ; the game's variable the ship-destroyed site wrote (LD ($8072),A), written here first
@equ $82E0 SelectionsText ; the game's argument the SELECTIONS site loaded (LD HL,$82E0)
@equ $91E2 SelectWeapon ; the game's routine the weapon-select site called
@equ $99A9 BombBounceStep ; the game's routine the bomb-bounce site called
@equ $9CB0 LaunchFromShip ; the game's routine the homing site called (the shared launch from the ship's place)
@equ $A423 ShowHonour ; the game's routine the role-of-honour site called
@equ $A489 TakePod ; the game's routine the pod-taken site called
@equ $A4EF DrawLives ; the game's routine the extra-life site called (the lives redrawn)
@equ $A595 HonourResult ; the game's routine the result site called
@equ $A685 ScreenWipe ; the game's routine both wipe sites called
@equ $D6ED ExplosionPattern ; the explosion's third pattern, loaded by the explosion site (LD HL,$D6ED)
@equ $F36F ShipPlace ; the ship's place, the argument the special-launch site loaded (LD HL,$F36F)
@const PAGE4 $14 ; $7FFD: bank 4 at $C000 (the engine), the 48 BASIC ROM, screen 0
@const PAGE0 $10 ; $7FFD: bank 0 at $C000 (the game)
@isub $B317 LD A,PAGE4
@isub $B319 LD BC,PORT_7FFD
@isub $B321 LD A,PAGE0
@isub $B323 LD BC,PORT_7FFD

@module stubs ; the 128K hook stubs: one engine sound at each event the 48K beeped at
@about The set-up copies the shared stub HookSound first, then the hooks one after another, writing each hook's address into its call site in the game as it goes (docs/03-build-and-load.md 3.5). A hook is the instruction its site lost (when the site was not the beeper call itself), PUSH HL, LD L with the low byte of an engine entry, and a jump to HookSound. HookSound writes $C9 and L into its own CALL, pages the engine in, calls it, pages the game back and returns with the caller's HL (the PUSH HL of the hook): the site goes on as before.
$B30D c HookSound ; page 4 in, CALL $C9xx (xx = L), page 0 back; HL from the stack, every other register kept
> Input: L = the engine entry's low byte, the caller's HL on the stack (pushed by the hook), the site's return address under it. The entry is written into the CALL's operand (EngineCall + 1, self-modifying). IX, AF, DE and BC are kept around the call; HL is the one the hook pushed. It does not disable interrupts.
$B312 ; IX, AF, DE, BC kept
$B317 ; page 4: the engine
$B31E EngineCall ; CALL $C9xx: the operand written above
$B321 ; page 0: the game
$B328 ; the registers back, HL the hook's
$B32F c HookShot ; the player fires (site $9C77, the beeper call): sound $0E
> Entry $C971. The site is the shot routine's CALL $B2F0 (48K sound 2) after it takes a free shot slot.
$B330 ; the low byte of the engine entry $C971
$B334 c HookExtraLife ; an extra life given (site $ACA2): CALL DrawLives, then sounds $0F + $10
> Entry $C975. $AC7A compares the score's second BCD byte with the $800F table (01 03 05 07 09 FF): a life at 10 000, 30 000, 50 000, 70 000 and 90 000 (INC (IX+12), INC (IX+4)); DrawLives redraws the ship icons first. Witnessed in r1 frame 6590 (docs/09-sound.md 9.2).
$B338 ; the low byte of the engine entry $C975
$B33C c HookBombBounce ; a plasma bomb bounces off the ground (site $9EC2): CALL BombBounceStep, then sound $11
> Entry $C97B. The bomb handler $9E67 negates and halves the vertical speed on a scenery hit and counts DEC (IY+38): three bounces, then the bomb is removed at $9ECE. Witnessed in r1, 22 frames from 1141.
$B340 ; the low byte of the engine entry $C97B
$B344 c HookHonour ; the role of honour shown (site $A81B): CALL ShowHonour, then sound $12
> Entry $C97F.
$B348 ; the low byte of the engine entry $C97F
$B34C c HookHonourResult ; the role of honour's result (site $A8B7): CALL HonourResult, then sounds $14 + $15
> Entry $C987.
$B350 ; the low byte of the engine entry $C987
$B354 c HookShipLost ; the player's ship destroyed (site $9BFF, which lost LD ($8072),A): the store, then sounds $14 + $15
> Entry $C987, the same as HookHonourResult's.
$B358 ; the low byte of the engine entry $C987
$B35C c HookHomingLaunch ; a homing missile launched (site $9CFA): CALL LaunchFromShip, then sounds $1A + $1B
> Entry $C98B. $9CCA runs while fire is held with a lock ($80E2 not 0); LaunchFromShip goes through HookSpecialLaunch, so a launch plays $18 and then $1A + $1B in the same tick. Witnessed in r2 frames 127 and 287.
$B360 ; the low byte of the engine entry $C98B
$B364 c HookPodTaken ; a pod taken, the highlight moves on (site $A247): CALL TakePod, then sound $16
> Entry $C991.
$B368 ; the low byte of the engine entry $C991
$B36C c HookSpecialLaunch ; a special weapon placed at the ship (site $9CB0, which lost LD HL,$F36F): the load, then sound $18
> Entry $C999. $9CB0 is the shared launch from the ship's place, reached from the plasma ($9C83, fire held 3 passes), the homing missiles ($9CFA) and the seekers ($9D1F). Witnessed in r1 (bombs, 9 frames from 1113) and r2 (homing).
$B370 ; the low byte of the engine entry $C999
$B374 c HookEnemyMissile ; an enemy fires a missile at the ship (site $A1C4, the beeper call): sound $19
> Entry $C99D.
$B375 ; the low byte of the engine entry $C99D
$B379 c HookWeaponSelect ; a weapon selected (site $A21A): CALL SelectWeapon, then sound $0F
> Entry $C9A1. A pod taken with fire held 8 passes or more ($8184 >= 8) runs the highlighted entry (player record +7) of the table at $80F0: 0 speed, 1 laser, 2 plasma, 3 homing, 4 seekers. Witnessed in r1 frames 1097 and 1713.
$B37D ; the low byte of the engine entry $C9A1
$B381 c HookPodAppears ; a pod appears (site $A31D, the beeper call): sound $1C
> Entry $C9A9. An object gets the pod descriptor $7EBB (29 times in r1).
$B382 ; the low byte of the engine entry $C9A9
$B386 c HookExplosion ; an explosion starts (site $A29F, which lost LD HL,ExplosionPattern): the load, then sound $1D
> Entry $C9AD.
$B38A ; the low byte of the engine entry $C9AD
$B38F c HookSelections ; the SELECTIONS screen (site $A7BB, which lost LD HL,$82E0): the music off, the load, sounds $1E + $1F
> Entry $C9B1. Key 1 or 2 on the title's credits page runs $A76F, then $A790; MusicSwitch with A = 0 stops the tune first. Witnessed in r1 frame 23.
$B397 ; the low byte of the engine entry $C9B1
$B39C c HookScreenWipe ; the screen wipe (sites $A5D1, title key 3 KEYBOARD DEFINITION, and $A7F7, the game over): the music off, CALL ScreenWipe, sounds $1E + $1F
> Entry $C9B1, the same as HookSelections's. Both sites are patched to this hook.
$B3A4 ; the low byte of the engine entry $C9B1
